      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:9:8:4",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ الْحَمَامُ يُرْسَلْنَ مِنَ الْمَوَاضِعِ الْبَعِيدَةِ فَيَأْتِي وَ يُرْسَلْنَ مِنَ الْمَكَانِ الْقَرِيبِ فَلَا يَأْتِي فَقَالَ إِذَا انْقَطَعَ أُكُلُهُ فَلَا يَأْتِي ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Al Husayn Bin Muhammad, from Moala Bin Muhammad, from Muhammad Bin Jamhour, from Ali Bin Dawood Al Haddad, from Hareyz, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I said, ‘The pigeons which are sent with a message from the remote places, so they come, and they are sent from the nearby places so they don’t come’. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘When its feed is cut-off, so they don’t come’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad has narrated from Mu‘alla’ ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Jumhur from Ali ibn Dawud al-Haddad from Hariz who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of birds that are set free in a faraway place come but not the ones released nearby. He (the Imam) said, ‘When its sustenance in the area is depleted, then it does not come back.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
